===== README.md =====
# fixture

A fixture project.

[![npm](https://img.shields.io/npm/v/fixture.svg)](https://www.npmjs.com/package/fixture) [![CI](https://github.com/fixture/fixture/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/fixture/fixture/actions/workflows/ci.yml) [![License: MIT](https://img.shields.io/badge/license-MIT-blue.svg)](LICENSE)

## Requirements

Node.js >= 24.0.0 (`.nvmrc` pins 24.18.0; run `nvm use`). Enforced via `engine-strict`, so installs fail fast on an unsupported version.

## Install

```sh
npm install fixture
```

## Usage

```ts
import { greet } from 'fixture';

greet('world'); // "Hello, world!"
```

## Continuous integration

The `CI` workflow runs typecheck, lint, tests, and build on every push. It uses `npm ci`, which needs a committed lockfile — so after creating the repo, run `npm install` and commit the generated `package-lock.json`. Until then CI fails with _"Dependencies lock file is not found"_ (expected on a brand-new repo).

